        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.purl.org/decide/LiveStockHealthOnto/LHO#CS65"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The prevalence of Bovine Respiratory Disease (BRD) in cattle varies significantly across different regions, age groups, and diagnostic methods. BRD is estimated to affect 2.1% to 20.2% of cattle, with higher rates observed in winter months. The disease is a leading cause of morbidity and mortality in pre-weaned dairy calves, and its economic impact is substantial, leading to mortality, reduced growth, and lower carcass value.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BRD_Prevalence</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


